    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-33002",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9927bff1-c245-542b-8d5d-fa7d24188b85",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given in Canonical Form",
      "problem": "Consider the straight line with the canonical equation $\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{1}=\\frac{z+7}{-5}.$ Find the vector equation of the line.",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{1}=\\frac{z-(-7)}{-5},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(3,1,-7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨5,1,-5⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "r=t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "r=t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )",
