    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-127461",
      "knowledge_point_id": "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Cartesian Equation of a Line When a Component of the Direction Vector is Zero",
      "problem": "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-5}=\\frac{y-0}{1}=\\frac{z-(-2)}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-5}=\\frac{y}{1}=\\frac{z+2}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z+2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=-2:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3-5t \\\\ t \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z+2}{0}$ part and instead write $z=-2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-5}=\\frac{y}{1},\\,z=-2\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{x-3}{-5}=\\frac{y}{1},\\,z=-2"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y}{2},\\,z=2"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y}{-1},\\,z=-2"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{x-5}{-3}=\\frac{y}{1},\\,z=-2"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{x+3}{-5}=\\frac{y}{1},\\,z=2"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "\\frac{x-3}{-5}=\\frac{y}{1},\\,z=-2",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
